ral-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Mississippi remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential elections, and fundamentals put the Republican nominee about eleven points ahead. No public polls of the state, expert ratings, or market prices are available, so the forecast rests almost entirely on partisan lean. The state backed Donald Trump by double digits in recent cycles, and no incumbent will be on the ballot.\n\nHeadlines about a possible Democratic surge in 2026 and Kamala Harris's campaign travels speak to the national climate rather than to Mississippi specifically. With no state-level evidence pointing either way, there is little reason to move off the fundamentals. The Republican nominee starts as a clear but not insurmountable favorite; a strong national Democratic wave could narrow the margin, though carrying the state would require an unusually large shift.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1069, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1631, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.153, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1578, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.153, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1586, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1588, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.158, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1552, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1593, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1587, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1556, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1596, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1637, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1463, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1535, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.1505, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.1622, "margin": -